<p>Now, let's say we're at some random index in the array, index <code>i</c=
ode>. An interesting observation is that if the next number (at index <code=
>i + 1</code>) is greater than the current, there=E2=80=99s definitely a lo=
cal maxima somewhere to the right of <code>i</code>. This is because the tw=
o points at index <code>i</code> and <code>i + 1</code> form an <strong>asc=
ending slope</strong>, and this slope would be heading upwards towards some=
 maxima:</p>
